# 🩺 CKD Prediction Web App

## 📊 Project Overview

The **CKD Prediction Web App** is a Machine Learning-based web application developed to predict the possibility of **Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)** using selected clinical parameters.

The project combines **Python, Machine Learning, Flask, SQLite, Flask-SQLAlchemy, HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and PDF reporting** into a complete web-based application.

The application provides an end-to-end workflow where clinical information is entered through a web interface, processed into the format expected by the trained Machine Learning model, and used to generate a CKD prediction.

The application also provides functionality for storing patient-related information, viewing records, and generating a PDF report.

### Workflow

**Clinical Data → Data Preprocessing → Machine Learning Model → Flask Application → Prediction → Patient Record → PDF Report**


# 🧩 Problem Statement

Chronic Kidney Disease can affect kidney function over time and may be associated with different clinical measurements.

When multiple clinical parameters are involved, analyzing these values manually can be difficult to manage within a software application.

This project focuses on developing a web-based Machine Learning application that accepts selected clinical parameters and passes them to a trained prediction model.

The application provides a structured interface for entering patient information and displaying the resulting prediction.

The system is developed as an **educational and demonstration project** to show how a trained Machine Learning model can be integrated into a practical Flask web application.

> ⚠️ **Important:** The prediction generated by this application is not intended to replace professional medical diagnosis or clinical decision-making.

# 🎯 Project Objectives

## 🤖 Machine Learning Objectives

The Machine Learning component of the project focuses on:

* Preparing the CKD dataset for model training
* Selecting the clinical parameters required by the model
* Preparing input features in the required format
* Training the Machine Learning model
* Saving the trained model as `model.pkl`
* Loading the saved model into the Flask application
* Generating predictions from user-entered clinical parameters
* Verifying the feature structure expected by the trained model

## 🌐 Web Application Objectives

The web application was developed to:

* Provide a web-based interface for the CKD prediction system
* Allow users to create an account
* Provide user sign-in functionality
* Collect patient clinical information through a form
* Send submitted information to the Machine Learning model
* Display the generated prediction
* Maintain patient-related records
* Generate PDF reports
* Provide an application settings page

## 🗄️ Database Objectives

The database component is used to:

* Store application-related information
* Store patient-related information
* Connect the Flask application with the database
* Define database models using Flask-SQLAlchemy
* Manage database changes using Flask-Migrate and Alembic



# 🗂️ Dataset

## CKD Dataset

The project uses a preprocessed CKD dataset stored in:

```text
CKD_Preprocessed.csv
```

The dataset contains the clinical parameters used as inputs for the Machine Learning model.

The trained model expects **12 input features**.

## Clinical Parameters

| Parameter                     | Description                 |
| ----------------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Age (yrs)                     | Patient age in years        |
| Blood Pressure (mm/Hg)        | Blood pressure measurement  |
| Specific Gravity              | Urine specific gravity      |
| Albumin                       | Albumin measurement         |
| Sugar                         | Sugar measurement           |
| Blood Glucose Random (mgs/dL) | Random blood glucose level  |
| Blood Urea (mgs/dL)           | Blood urea level            |
| Serum Creatinine (mgs/dL)     | Serum creatinine level      |
| Hemoglobin (gms)              | Hemoglobin level            |
| Hypertension: yes             | Hypertension indicator      |
| Diabetes Mellitus: yes        | Diabetes mellitus indicator |
| Anemia: yes                   | Anemia indicator            |

These are the feature names verified from the saved Machine Learning model.



# 🧹 Data Preprocessing

Before the dataset can be used by the Machine Learning model, the required clinical information needs to be prepared in the expected format.

The preprocessing workflow includes:

* Loading the CKD dataset
* Preparing the required clinical features
* Selecting the features required by the prediction model
* Preparing categorical health indicators for model use
* Converting model inputs into the required format
* Maintaining the same feature structure expected during prediction
* Saving the prepared dataset as `CKD_Preprocessed.csv`

### Final Model Input Features

```text
Age (yrs)
Blood Pressure (mm/Hg)
Specific Gravity
Albumin
Sugar
Blood Glucose Random (mgs/dL)
Blood Urea (mgs/dL)
Serum Creatinine (mgs/dL)
Hemoglobin (gms)
Hypertension: yes
Diabetes Mellitus: yes
Anemia: yes
```

Maintaining the same feature names and order during prediction is important because the Flask application uses the saved model trained with this feature structure.



# 🤖 Machine Learning Model

## Model Training

The Machine Learning training process is implemented in:

```text
train_model.py
```

The trained Machine Learning model is saved as:

```text
model.pkl
```

The Flask application loads this saved model rather than training the model every time the web application starts.

